%description:

Tests that a socket command which reaches an Ieee8021qProtocol without socket
support (hasSocketSupport = false, the default) stops the simulation with an
error. The VirtualTunnel of a virtual interface with a VLAN ID binds an
Ieee8021qSocket at initialization. Without socket support, the protocol has no
socket command processor, so the BIND request reaches the tag header inserter.

Before the inserter rejected socket commands, it passed the request down to
the node's dispatcher, which dispatched it to the ieee8021qctag service, back
up to the same protocol, and the request circled at t = 0 until the CPU time
limit ended the run.

%# expected-result: FAIL

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
include ../../lib/socket-command.ini

*.*.ieee8021q.typename = "Ieee8021qProtocol"
*.host2.numVirtInterfaces = 1
*.host2.virt[0].tunnel.realInterface = "eth0"
*.host2.virt[0].tunnel.vlanId = 42

%subst: /\x1B\[[0-9;]*m//
%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep "<!>" test.* > test_err.out || true
%contains: test_err.out
Received socket command BIND, but the protocol layer has no socket support (hasSocketSupport = false)
